{"title":"Career Roadmap · R&D Chemist","role":"R&D Chemist","summary":"An R&D Chemist works on discovering, developing, testing, optimizing, and characterizing chemical products, materials, formulations, and processes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An R&D Chemist works on discovering, developing, testing, optimizing, and characterizing chemical products, materials, formulations, and processes."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing experiments"},{"text":"Chemical synthesis"},{"text":"Formulation development"},{"text":"Analytical testing"},{"text":"Material characterization"},{"text":"Process optimization"},{"text":"Failure/root-cause analysis"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"},{"text":"Data interpretation"},{"text":"Scale-up support"},{"text":"Research reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Chemistry student, the strongest long-term pathway is generally:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Chemistry","M.Sc Chemistry / Applied Chemistry","R&D / Research Role","Specialized Chemist","Senior R&D Scientist"]},{"type":"p","text":"An M.Sc is particularly valuable for moving from routine laboratory work toward independent R&D and advanced scientific positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Chemistry, laboratory fundamentals, analytical techniques, research projects"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"M.Sc Chemistry / specialization, research internship, R&D/analytical roles"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"R&D Chemist / Scientist, product and process development"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Scientist, Principal Scientist, R&D Lead, Technical Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During